# Files in `app/` that are NOT part of the published site.
#
# The served app is `app/`, so this file is the whole answer to "what is
# downloadable" for the new build. It mirrors the repository root's
# `.assetsignore`, but for the app directory: the shared stager
# (tools/deploy-pages.mjs) reads the ignore file FROM THE ASSETS DIRECTORY it
# is given, so without this one the TypeScript source, the type definitions
# and the build tooling would all be published.
#
# `dist/` is deliberately NOT here: it holds the built bundle, which is the
# one file the document actually loads.

# The typed logic core and the sources. The bundle is what ships; the source
# is not.
src/
lib/
hairline/

# Build tooling.
package.json
package-lock.json
tsconfig.json
node_modules/

# The accessibility harness: it drives the real app in a visible frame, so it
# is a laptop tool like the roster harness above and never part of the deploy.
a11y-harness.html

# The dev server's own files.
serve.sh
scripts/

# The app's own README and docs, if it grows any.
README.md
CLAUDE.md

# A local dump of a spreadsheet somebody pasted in. It must never be served,
# even committed by accident: it is somebody's pay.
*.csv
*.xlsx
tesco_full.txt
